The old plan was marked outdated, and the code has moved well past it. All ten points of the ticket's summary already work on `main`:
- the scheduler resumes runs named by a check;
- the GitHub check (`replies`) covers comments, reviews, red checks and conflicts;
- the `reply` skill exists;
- a run whose conversation is gone starts over with its earlier record and pull request attached;
- `/agent` on an issue or pull request no agent is on starts a new run.

